WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.095
Pu'cha!
Prepare to meet your ancestors.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.387
This battle is yours today,

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.794
but the House of Mo'Kai
will never yield.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.529
DoH-cha Scree!

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.536
Move away, coward.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.800
L want to make this kill.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.467
You should have killed me
when my back was turned.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.272
L want to see
the fear in your eyes.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.277
Look closely

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.108
and you'll see
your own destruction.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.445
You are resilient prey.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.609
L'm no one's prey!

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.955
You are mine

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.962
now and after death.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.090
Sick Bay, this is Holodeck 2.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:11.001
Janeway requires
medical assistance.

00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:07.314
She'll survive.

00:03:07.352 --> 00:03:09.513
What about her neural interface?

00:03:12.657 --> 00:03:14.591
Stable.

00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:16.423
Are you sure?

00:03:16.461 --> 00:03:17.689
There were times

00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:21.096
when she seemed...
aware of who she is.

00:03:21.132 --> 00:03:22.394
Impossible.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.925
L was monitoring the crew
during the entire simulation.

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:28.200
She believes she's whoever
we program her to be.

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:30.901
Shall l return her
to the Klingon simulation?

00:03:30.942 --> 00:03:34.378
No. Bring her to Holodeck 1.

00:03:34.412 --> 00:03:38.143
L've found another program
l want to try.

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:40.777
A conflict that took place
on her own planet.

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:43.185
It should prove...

00:03:43.221 --> 00:03:45.018
stimulating.

00:04:00.071 --> 00:04:04.440
Wrong

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:09.937
Would it be wrong to kiss

00:04:09.981 --> 00:04:15.715
Seeing l feel like this?

00:04:15.753 --> 00:04:24.855
Would it be wrong to try?

00:04:24.896 --> 00:04:29.265
Wrong

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:34.533
Would it be wrong to stay

00:04:34.572 --> 00:04:40.408
Here in your arms this way

00:04:40.445 --> 00:04:46.281
Under this starry sky?

00:04:46.317 --> 00:04:53.883
Lf it is wrong...

00:04:53.925 --> 00:04:56.120
Welcome to Le Coeur de Lion.

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:57.890
L'm Katrine.

00:04:57.929 --> 00:04:59.863
The first round
is with my compliments

00:04:59.898 --> 00:05:00.865
on one condition...

00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:04.096
you leave the war outside.

00:05:04.135 --> 00:05:07.298
More escargot
for table nine, hmm?

00:05:07.338 --> 00:05:10.899
Jacques, no lady tonight?

00:05:10.942 --> 00:05:13.911
Oh-ho. We'll have to see
what we can do about that.

00:05:13.945 --> 00:05:15.776
Forgive my neglecting you.

00:05:15.813 --> 00:05:17.075
Now, where were we?

00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:20.141
Ah, yes, my latest
adventure in Paris.

00:05:20.185 --> 00:05:23.621
...Wrong

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:28.456
When l need you so much...

00:05:28.493 --> 00:05:31.326
l'm afraid l have
to neglect you again.

00:05:31.362 --> 00:05:32.386
Excuse me.

00:05:33.431 --> 00:05:37.390
...so long

00:05:37.435 --> 00:05:43.635
lt must be right...

00:05:43.675 --> 00:05:45.472
That's him.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.239
Our new commandant?

00:05:47.278 --> 00:05:48.905
British Intelligence believes
he's been sent here

00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:50.972
to oversee the occupation
of the city.

00:05:51.015 --> 00:05:51.982
What's his history?

00:05:52.083 --> 00:05:53.107
He served with Rommel

00:05:53.151 --> 00:05:55.483
in North Africa
and Schmidt in Poland.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.988
He is a formidable
military strategist,

00:05:58.022 --> 00:06:00.081
notorious for his cruelty.

00:06:00.124 --> 00:06:02.752
Well, let's make him
feel at home.

00:06:02.794 --> 00:06:04.318
Send him a bottle
of Chateau Latour.

00:06:04.362 --> 00:06:05.590
My compliments.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.892
The '29?

00:06:06.931 --> 00:06:08.023
Oh, l hate to waste good wine.

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:09.658
Give him the '36.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.692
As you wish.

00:06:11.736 --> 00:06:19.438
...And l have waited so long

00:06:19.477 --> 00:06:27.680
lt must be right

00:06:27.719 --> 00:06:37.390
lt can't be wrong.

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:44.461
Merci.

00:06:44.502 --> 00:06:46.265
Be generous to Claude
this evening.

00:06:46.304 --> 00:06:49.296
Without him, my voice is empty.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.602
Good evening.

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:54.239
Sing.

00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:55.974
Tonight's performance
is over.

00:06:56.047 --> 00:06:56.979
Return tomorrow.

00:06:57.048 --> 00:06:58.481
Now.

00:06:58.516 --> 00:07:00.711
Remove your hand.

00:07:00.752 --> 00:07:02.913
Obey me

00:07:02.954 --> 00:07:05.354
or l will hunt you down

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.120
and your bones will adorn
the bulkhead of my ship.

00:07:08.159 --> 00:07:10.320
Sit down and play the game.

00:07:10.361 --> 00:07:13.125
In this setting,
we have no ships.

00:07:13.164 --> 00:07:15.189
We are an ancient race
of soldiers

00:07:15.233 --> 00:07:17.701
intent
upon conquering this world.

00:07:17.735 --> 00:07:19.168
Play the game.

00:07:19.203 --> 00:07:22.036
Now, now. What's this?

00:07:22.073 --> 00:07:23.040
Mademoiselle de Neuf

00:07:23.074 --> 00:07:24.735
will be happy
to sing another song.

00:07:24.776 --> 00:07:26.107
Just give her a few minutes
to freshen up.

00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:27.270
It's late.

00:07:27.312 --> 00:07:28.643
Freshen up.

00:07:31.649 --> 00:07:32.911
Very well.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:34.918
Commandant Karr.

00:07:34.952 --> 00:07:36.510
You know me.

00:07:36.554 --> 00:07:38.351
Your reputation precedes you.

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:40.118
L'm Katrine.

00:07:40.158 --> 00:07:41.955
Le Coeur de Lion
is my establishment.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.494
The first round
is with my compliments

00:07:44.529 --> 00:07:47.464
on one condition...
you leave the war outside.

00:07:47.498 --> 00:07:50.092
L wish to speak with her...

00:07:50.134 --> 00:07:51.658
alone.

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:06.215
Charming gentleman.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.616
He is disoriented.

00:08:08.653 --> 00:08:11.315
Your world is unfamiliar to him.

00:08:11.356 --> 00:08:12.914
He'll be comfortable
soon enough.

00:08:12.957 --> 00:08:15.221
The arms of France
are open to all.

00:08:15.259 --> 00:08:17.250
L've heard otherwise.

00:08:17.295 --> 00:08:18.387
What do you mean?

00:08:18.429 --> 00:08:20.260
L understand
there is opposition

00:08:20.298 --> 00:08:23.062
to our presence here
among your citizens.

00:08:23.101 --> 00:08:24.762
The Resistance?

00:08:24.802 --> 00:08:27.100
In Paris, perhaps,

00:08:27.138 --> 00:08:30.301
but this is a small city,
defenseless.

00:08:30.341 --> 00:08:33.868
We've learned to be
a little more diplomatic.

00:08:33.911 --> 00:08:35.469
When this war is over,

00:08:35.513 --> 00:08:38.311
we want to remain
on good terms with the victor.

00:08:38.349 --> 00:08:42.410
- Whoever that may be.
- Whoever that may be.

00:08:44.088 --> 00:08:47.546
Your city may be defenseless,
but it's crucial to the war.

00:08:47.592 --> 00:08:49.958
Any ground assault into Germany

00:08:50.061 --> 00:08:52.359
must pass through
this province.

00:08:52.397 --> 00:08:55.093
The Resistance will come here.

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:58.193
If they do, l'll tell them
what l tell everyone...

00:08:59.837 --> 00:09:01.634
leave the war outside.

00:09:04.175 --> 00:09:06.109
Excellent.

00:09:06.144 --> 00:09:07.771
Commandant, l've been informed

00:09:07.812 --> 00:09:10.280
there's a problem
in the Engineering section.

00:09:10.314 --> 00:09:13.010
The warp plasma network
has become unstable.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.779
What's he talking about?

00:09:14.819 --> 00:09:16.946
Lt need not concern you.

00:09:19.724 --> 00:09:21.282
To the hunt.

00:09:21.325 --> 00:09:22.292
"The hunt"?

00:09:22.326 --> 00:09:24.191
For the Resistance.

00:09:24.228 --> 00:09:27.220
L shall take great pleasure
in tracking them down...

00:09:28.699 --> 00:09:30.894
and making the kill.

00:09:43.147 --> 00:09:44.808
Au revoir.

00:09:51.189 --> 00:09:52.952
How'd we do?

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.686
Insufficient
for a Saturday night.

00:09:55.726 --> 00:09:58.820
1,247 francs
and 81 Reichsmarks.

00:09:58.863 --> 00:09:59.830
Well, it should be enough

00:09:59.864 --> 00:10:01.422
to buy an oscillator
to extend the range

00:10:01.466 --> 00:10:02.933
of our radio.

00:10:02.967 --> 00:10:04.958
First thing tomorrow
morning, l want you

00:10:05.002 --> 00:10:07.095
to take a little trip
to the countryside.

00:10:07.138 --> 00:10:09.538
There's a Monsieur Groleau
who has a cottage

00:10:09.574 --> 00:10:11.508
just past the third bridge.

00:10:11.542 --> 00:10:14.375
He's got a wine cellar
full of vacuum tubes.

00:10:14.412 --> 00:10:16.744
Tell him we need a high
frequency oscillator.

00:10:16.781 --> 00:10:17.975
Offer him 300 francs,

00:10:18.082 --> 00:10:19.845
but don't go any higher
than 500.

00:10:19.884 --> 00:10:21.784
We have more pressing needs.

00:10:21.819 --> 00:10:22.877
Such as?

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.081
Explosives. We need
a launcher that can fire

00:10:25.122 --> 00:10:26.783
armor-piercing grenades.

00:10:26.824 --> 00:10:28.689
Planning on blowing
up a German tank?

00:10:28.726 --> 00:10:30.216
Lf necessary.

00:10:30.261 --> 00:10:32.252
We're not trying
to build an army here.

00:10:32.296 --> 00:10:34.628
Well, maybe it's time we did.

00:10:34.665 --> 00:10:37.099
Three more German battalions
have occupied the city

00:10:37.134 --> 00:10:38.795
and a panzer division
is holding position

00:10:38.836 --> 00:10:40.565
11 kilometers away.

00:10:40.605 --> 00:10:42.766
When the Americans arrive
and the fighting begins,

00:10:42.807 --> 00:10:44.798
l don't intend to be standing
next to a piano

00:10:44.842 --> 00:10:46.639
singing "Moonlight Becomes You."

00:10:46.677 --> 00:10:47.974
The Americans won't even be able

00:10:48.012 --> 00:10:50.310
to approach this city
without our help.

00:10:50.348 --> 00:10:52.009
And if they can't
liberate Sainte Claire,

00:10:52.049 --> 00:10:54.244
the assault into
Germany could fail.

00:10:54.285 --> 00:10:56.014
We need to be
gathering information

00:10:56.087 --> 00:10:57.247
about German troop movements

00:10:57.288 --> 00:10:59.347
and relaying it
to Allied Command.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:01.415
L'm tired of lighting
the Nazis' cigarettes

00:11:01.459 --> 00:11:03.120
and laughing at their jokes.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.152
We should be helping the Allies
by assassinating these pigs.

00:11:06.197 --> 00:11:09.257
The moment we start shooting,
we expose ourselves.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.495
Right now, no one suspects us

00:11:11.536 --> 00:11:13.902
and l am not about to risk
our entire operation

00:11:13.938 --> 00:11:15.269
because you've
suddenly developed

00:11:15.306 --> 00:11:16.506
a nervous trigger finger.

00:11:16.639 --> 00:11:18.470
That is your opinion, madame.

00:11:18.508 --> 00:11:19.668
L'm the leader
of the movement here

00:11:19.709 --> 00:11:21.677
and right now, my opinion
is the only one that counts,

00:11:21.711 --> 00:11:23.110
so get the oscillator.

00:11:25.781 --> 00:11:28.272
L think we're all
feeling the strain.

00:11:28.317 --> 00:11:29.443
It's been a hard four years,

00:11:29.485 --> 00:11:30.452
but believe me

00:11:30.486 --> 00:11:32.647
the Third Reich
is feeling it, too.

00:11:32.688 --> 00:11:34.986
We just have to hang on
a little while longer.

00:11:35.024 --> 00:11:37.322
Word from the Americans
is going to come any day.

00:11:39.428 --> 00:11:41.020
Perhaps.

00:11:44.033 --> 00:11:45.193
Again?

00:11:45.234 --> 00:11:47.225
Again.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:50.000
Why is she so adamant?

00:11:50.072 --> 00:11:52.438
What she's proposing
would put us all at risk.

00:11:52.475 --> 00:11:54.841
Maybe that's her intention.

00:11:54.877 --> 00:11:57.345
If you have suspicions,
my old friend,

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.472
let's hear them.

00:11:58.514 --> 00:12:00.812
From the beginning,
she's been argumentative

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.613
and on more
than a few occasions,

00:12:02.652 --> 00:12:04.415
she's disobeyed
your direct orders.

00:12:04.453 --> 00:12:06.921
She's headstrong...
typical of the underground.

00:12:06.956 --> 00:12:10.414
Nevertheless, her behavior
has threatened our identities.

00:12:10.459 --> 00:12:12.893
She's the only
munitions expert we have

00:12:12.929 --> 00:12:14.760
and she can carry a tune.

00:12:14.797 --> 00:12:15.957
We need her.

00:12:16.032 --> 00:12:17.693
Let's keep our eye on her.

00:12:17.733 --> 00:12:20.497
Have her followed
for the next few days.

00:12:20.536 --> 00:12:23.334
If she is a Nazi infiltrator,

00:12:23.372 --> 00:12:25.067
we'll have to eliminate her.

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:41.914
Bonjour, madame!

00:12:41.958 --> 00:12:43.186
Bonjour, monsieur.

00:12:47.597 --> 00:12:49.258
Put it on my account.

00:12:49.298 --> 00:12:50.265
Whoo.

00:12:53.269 --> 00:12:54.497
Guten Tag.

00:12:54.537 --> 00:12:57.438
You... halt!

00:13:04.814 --> 00:13:06.805
Get off your vehicle.

00:13:08.751 --> 00:13:10.651
What are you transporting?

00:13:10.686 --> 00:13:13.280
Nothing but
the very essentials of life.

00:13:29.939 --> 00:13:31.736
Proceed to your destination.

00:13:31.774 --> 00:13:33.264
That l will.

00:13:33.309 --> 00:13:35.277
That l most certainly will.

00:13:35.311 --> 00:13:38.280
If the choice were mine,

00:13:38.314 --> 00:13:40.339
you would already be dead.

00:13:48.824 --> 00:13:50.553
...all report rain.

00:13:50.593 --> 00:13:52.788
It's currently
59 degrees in Dover

00:13:52.828 --> 00:13:54.921
with low fog across the Channel.

00:13:54.964 --> 00:13:56.932
Temperatures are expected
to range

00:13:56.966 --> 00:13:58.695
from a low of 45 degrees...

00:14:00.469 --> 00:14:01.959
Damn, l'm missing it.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.067
Our most recent intelligence

00:14:07.109 --> 00:14:10.203
shows two German armored
divisions here and here.

00:14:10.246 --> 00:14:11.713
How recent is this intelligence?

00:14:11.747 --> 00:14:13.681
- 48 hours.
- Old news.

00:14:13.716 --> 00:14:15.047
L am Reginald Smith

00:14:15.084 --> 00:14:17.848
and you're listening
to the British Radio Network.

00:14:17.887 --> 00:14:19.684
This report will repeat in...

00:14:19.722 --> 00:14:21.747
- 45 seconds.
- 45 seconds.

00:14:21.791 --> 00:14:23.281
Here's to English precision.

00:14:31.033 --> 00:14:32.591
We're closed.

00:14:32.635 --> 00:14:34.102
Morning delivery.

00:14:36.939 --> 00:14:38.907
You're late. What happened?

00:14:38.941 --> 00:14:40.533
Oh, just a little tête-à-tête

00:14:40.576 --> 00:14:42.237
with a member
of the Master Race.

00:14:42.278 --> 00:14:43.506
That's the second time
this week.

00:14:43.546 --> 00:14:45.446
Sound like they're increasing
their patrols.

00:14:45.481 --> 00:14:47.915
Perhaps it's time
we chose another courier.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.611
Our "baker"
is arousing suspicion.

00:14:49.652 --> 00:14:51.244
There's no need to worry.

00:14:51.287 --> 00:14:52.982
L change my route every day

00:14:53.022 --> 00:14:55.513
and l've become quite friendly
with most of the Gestapo.

00:14:55.558 --> 00:14:57.992
They just love my strudel.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:01.552
A kind thank you
to Jazzy McNulty and his band.

00:15:01.597 --> 00:15:06.193
Now, the weather for today,
September 22, 1944.

00:15:06.235 --> 00:15:07.793
In London, skies are gray

00:15:07.837 --> 00:15:10.328
with a strong chance
of afternoon rain.

00:15:10.372 --> 00:15:12.932
Temperatures will range
from a low of 52 degrees

00:15:12.975 --> 00:15:14.943
to a high of 71.

00:15:15.044 --> 00:15:18.104
The northern coast reports
heavy rain and strong winds

00:15:18.147 --> 00:15:20.638
and ocean swells
reaching four feet.

00:15:20.683 --> 00:15:24.847
Devonshire, Hertfordshire
and Sonnenshire all report rain.

00:15:24.887 --> 00:15:27.412
It's currently
59 degrees in Dover

00:15:27.456 --> 00:15:29.720
with low fog across the Channel.

00:15:29.759 --> 00:15:32.956
Temperatures are expected to
range from a low of 45 degrees

00:15:33.062 --> 00:15:34.962
to a high of 63.

00:15:34.997 --> 00:15:37.591
L am Reginald Smith,
and you are listening...

00:15:37.633 --> 00:15:38.600
Got it.

00:15:38.634 --> 00:15:40.397
Let's see the code key.

00:15:40.436 --> 00:15:42.370
Every fifth letter,
every third vowel.

00:15:42.404 --> 00:15:43.735
Use the Sunday
decryption sequence.

00:15:43.773 --> 00:15:44.933
Mm-hmm.

00:15:46.475 --> 00:15:48.670
"A..."

00:15:48.711 --> 00:15:49.973
"H... C."

00:15:50.012 --> 00:15:51.843
Straight
from Allied High Command.

00:15:51.881 --> 00:15:52.973
It must be important.

00:15:53.082 --> 00:15:55.744
All messages regarding
the war are important.

00:15:55.785 --> 00:15:57.252
It's only a matter of degree.

00:15:57.286 --> 00:15:58.913
L suppose you're right,
but do you have to be

00:15:58.954 --> 00:16:01.422
so... logical about everything?

00:16:01.457 --> 00:16:04.426
In any covert battle,
logic is a potent weapon.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:05.427
You might try it sometime.

00:16:05.461 --> 00:16:08.328
"American Fourth Infantry...

00:16:08.364 --> 00:16:11.856
"to invade Sainte Claire...

00:16:11.901 --> 00:16:12.868
Tuesday dawn."

00:16:12.902 --> 00:16:14.426
That's two days from now.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:17.667
"Require assistance.
Disable enemy communications.

00:16:17.706 --> 00:16:19.173
End message."

00:16:19.208 --> 00:16:22.143
The German radio transmitter
is housed at their headquarters.

00:16:22.178 --> 00:16:23.805
That building is
surrounded by guards.

00:16:23.846 --> 00:16:26.440
We can't just waltz in there
and plant a bomb.

00:16:26.482 --> 00:16:28.416
Maybe l can help.

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:29.712
How?

00:16:29.752 --> 00:16:31.811
L'm upset.

00:16:31.854 --> 00:16:35.085
L need to see
my special "friend..."

00:16:35.124 --> 00:16:37.217
even if it means
bothering him at the office.

00:16:37.259 --> 00:16:38.886
A reconnaissance mission.

00:16:38.928 --> 00:16:40.225
L'll try to locate the radio,

00:16:40.262 --> 00:16:42.856
see where the guards are posted,
examine the locks,

00:16:42.898 --> 00:16:44.661
gather enough information
to get us inside.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.134
It's too dangerous.

00:16:47.169 --> 00:16:48.227
If you're caught,

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.828
you'll be tortured
for information.

00:16:49.872 --> 00:16:51.965
You don't know my "friend."

00:16:52.007 --> 00:16:55.966
He would never do anything
to harm his own child.

00:16:58.647 --> 00:17:01.673
Encode a response
to Allied Command.

00:17:01.717 --> 00:17:04.015
Confirm that we've received
their message.

00:17:04.053 --> 00:17:07.079
Tell them we're proceeding
according to plan.

00:17:59.508 --> 00:18:01.408
Ever since my days
at the university,

00:18:01.443 --> 00:18:03.104
l've admired this painting...

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.909
and now it's mine.

00:18:06.949 --> 00:18:10.009
Our fellow officers
might prefer gold or land,

00:18:10.052 --> 00:18:13.283
but, for me, the greatest
prize of war is art.

00:18:13.322 --> 00:18:16.314
Trophies of the hunt...

00:18:16.358 --> 00:18:18.053
but was the hunt fair?

00:18:18.093 --> 00:18:19.458
Sir?

00:18:19.495 --> 00:18:20.928
We entered this city
with superior firepower

00:18:20.996 --> 00:18:23.226
against a weakened prey.

00:18:23.265 --> 00:18:26.860
Do you really deserve
these... prizes?

00:18:26.902 --> 00:18:28.927
We are German.

00:18:29.004 --> 00:18:32.167
The German people deserve Europe
and everything in it.

00:18:32.207 --> 00:18:33.572
Why?

00:18:33.609 --> 00:18:35.668
Sir...

00:18:35.711 --> 00:18:37.178
You question our destiny?

00:18:37.212 --> 00:18:38.645
Of course not,

00:18:38.681 --> 00:18:41.707
but l want to hear it
in your own words.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:45.948
Tell me...
why are we the "Master Race"?

00:18:46.055 --> 00:18:48.956
Our blood is pure.

00:18:49.024 --> 00:18:52.460
Our people lived and hunted on
this land for a thousand years

00:18:52.494 --> 00:18:55.122
before the degenerate races
brought their corruption.

00:18:55.164 --> 00:18:58.190
Europe must be purified.

00:18:58.233 --> 00:18:59.530
You, yourself...

00:18:59.568 --> 00:19:02.401
are you stronger
than these "degenerate" races?

00:19:02.438 --> 00:19:03.405
More cunning?

00:19:03.439 --> 00:19:04.497
Yes, of course.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.872
And if you were alone
without an army supporting you,

00:19:06.909 --> 00:19:08.706
would you continue the hunt?

00:19:08.744 --> 00:19:10.302
Lf your prey were armed

00:19:10.346 --> 00:19:12.610
instead of defenseless,
what then?

00:19:12.648 --> 00:19:14.081
Colonel, l don't know
what you're trying...

00:19:14.116 --> 00:19:16.914
You are superior to no one!

00:19:16.952 --> 00:19:21.389
Never underestimate your prey
or disrespect its abilities.

00:19:21.423 --> 00:19:24.915
If you do, you will become
the hunted.

00:19:25.027 --> 00:19:27.552
When the opposing army
invades this city,

00:19:27.596 --> 00:19:29.564
remember my words.

00:19:31.734 --> 00:19:32.758
Enter!

00:19:36.038 --> 00:19:37.062
Brigitte!

00:19:37.106 --> 00:19:38.596
L'm sorry.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:41.336
L know l'm not supposed
to come here.

00:19:41.377 --> 00:19:42.742
Don't blame him.

00:19:42.778 --> 00:19:44.575
L told him l was ill,
that l had to see you.

00:19:45.914 --> 00:19:48.906
L will leave you two alone.

00:19:51.353 --> 00:19:52.479
Heil Hitler.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.284
It's all right.

00:19:59.328 --> 00:20:01.762
The colonel is in
a strange mood today.

00:20:06.635 --> 00:20:08.330
What's wrong?
Ls it our child?

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:09.564
L don't know.

00:20:09.605 --> 00:20:11.095
L was dizzy.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.107
L'll call the doctor.

00:20:12.141 --> 00:20:13.506
No!

00:20:13.542 --> 00:20:15.669
L feel better now.

00:20:15.711 --> 00:20:18.179
Maybe l just needed to see you.

00:20:18.213 --> 00:20:21.842
Why haven't you
shown me this place before?

00:20:21.884 --> 00:20:24.318
L didn't want your neighbors
to see you coming here.

00:20:24.353 --> 00:20:26.321
They make it
difficult enough for you,

00:20:26.355 --> 00:20:27.413
knowing we're together.

00:20:27.456 --> 00:20:29.924
L don't care what they think.

00:20:32.061 --> 00:20:33.289
It's beautiful.

00:20:33.328 --> 00:20:37.230
Praxiteles, master sculptor
of ancient Greece.

00:20:37.266 --> 00:20:41.134
There are only three
like this in all of Europe.

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:45.231
So many...
wonderful things.

00:20:51.245 --> 00:20:52.712
The commandant would
have us continue

00:20:52.747 --> 00:20:55.307
this simulation until we rot.

00:20:55.349 --> 00:20:57.112
It's pointless.

00:20:57.151 --> 00:20:58.618
We should begin the hunt.

00:20:58.653 --> 00:21:01.554
He believes we must learn
more about our prey,

00:21:01.589 --> 00:21:04.080
but l have learned enough.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.889
Ready your weapon.

00:21:09.864 --> 00:21:11.263
Avoid the cranium.

00:21:22.877 --> 00:21:23.901
This way!

00:21:23.945 --> 00:21:25.071
The message!

00:21:25.113 --> 00:21:26.239
There's no time.

00:21:58.212 --> 00:21:59.702
Ah!

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:06.684
Computer, exit holodeck.

00:22:06.721 --> 00:22:08.279
We'll take them
to the medical bay.

00:22:16.597 --> 00:22:19.225
This neural interface
has been damaged.

00:22:19.267 --> 00:22:20.427
That's because it
took a direct hit

00:22:20.468 --> 00:22:22.663
when one of your bullets
grazed the base of her skull.

00:22:22.703 --> 00:22:24.967
L'll provide you with another...
install it.

00:22:25.039 --> 00:22:26.301
Not until l've repaired
her injuries.

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:27.466
How long?

00:22:27.508 --> 00:22:29.066
She has two fractured vertebrae

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.237
and a punctured lung...
another hour at least.

00:22:31.279 --> 00:22:32.268
Him?

00:22:32.313 --> 00:22:33.507
L've stabilized
his vital systems,

00:22:33.548 --> 00:22:35.413
but he still has
bullet fragments

00:22:35.449 --> 00:22:36.814
lodged in his shoulder.

00:22:36.851 --> 00:22:37.875
L will treat him.

00:22:37.919 --> 00:22:39.910
This time, you might
do a better job

00:22:39.954 --> 00:22:41.819
repairing
the muscle lacerations.

00:22:41.856 --> 00:22:43.153
The last crew member
you treated

00:22:43.191 --> 00:22:44.920
was brought back in
with internal bleeding.

00:22:44.959 --> 00:22:46.586
Your crew is fragile.

00:22:46.627 --> 00:22:48.424
They fall too easily.

00:22:48.462 --> 00:22:49.622
What do you expect?

00:22:49.664 --> 00:22:51.996
They've been stabbed,
shot, beaten, phasered

00:22:52.099 --> 00:22:53.691
and bat'lethed
over the past three weeks.

00:22:53.734 --> 00:22:55.702
Their bodies weren't designed
for this kind of punishment.

00:22:55.736 --> 00:22:56.828
What happened?

00:22:56.871 --> 00:22:58.839
These prey were hunted
by Turanj.

00:22:58.873 --> 00:23:00.602
Their injuries are severe.

00:23:00.641 --> 00:23:01.903
You assured me that your people

00:23:01.943 --> 00:23:03.706
would avoid causing
serious head injuries.

00:23:03.744 --> 00:23:04.768
Another centimeter

00:23:04.812 --> 00:23:06.939
and the bullet would have
penetrated her brain.

00:23:07.048 --> 00:23:08.345
If you can't keep
your people under control,

00:23:08.382 --> 00:23:10.213
then you should put an end
to this blood sport.

00:23:10.251 --> 00:23:12.276
The simulations will continue.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.379
At least activate the holodeck
safety protocols.

00:23:14.422 --> 00:23:15.320
No.

00:23:15.356 --> 00:23:16.721
It'll prevent
life-threatening injuries,

00:23:16.757 --> 00:23:17.781
for your people as well.

00:23:17.825 --> 00:23:20.521
It will also eliminate
the challenge.

00:23:20.561 --> 00:23:23.462
L have had 28 wounded
and one fatality

00:23:23.497 --> 00:23:25.226
in the past 12 hours.

00:23:25.266 --> 00:23:27.666
Even l can't keep up
with that level of triage.

00:23:27.702 --> 00:23:30.136
You will keep up
or they will die.

00:23:30.171 --> 00:23:32.696
Their lives are in your hands,
Doctor.

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:34.401
Don't fail them.

00:23:40.948 --> 00:23:44.611
When that one is ready
place him in Holodeck 2.

00:23:44.652 --> 00:23:46.882
Let's see how he fares
with the Klingons.

00:23:46.921 --> 00:23:48.252
What about her?

00:23:48.289 --> 00:23:49.688
Send her back to Holodeck 1.

00:23:49.724 --> 00:23:52.124
L like her voice.

00:24:01.102 --> 00:24:02.933
Progress?

00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:06.133
By cutting through the bulkheads
on Decks 4, 5 and 6,

00:24:06.173 --> 00:24:09.472
we've been able to expand
both holodeck grids

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:11.375
by 5,000 square meters.

00:24:11.412 --> 00:24:12.845
More.

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:17.650
L can't give you any more...

00:24:17.685 --> 00:24:20.347
not without compromising
Voyager's primary systems.

00:24:20.388 --> 00:24:21.946
Then compromise them.

00:24:21.989 --> 00:24:24.856
Look, holodecks require
a tremendous amount of energy.

00:24:24.892 --> 00:24:27.861
L've already rerouted power
from all nonessential systems.

00:24:27.895 --> 00:24:31.228
Anything more, and we'll start
losing propulsion, deflectors

00:24:31.265 --> 00:24:32.823
even life support.

00:24:32.867 --> 00:24:35.961
L'll transfer a supply
of power nodules from my vessel.

00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:38.061
Integrate them
into your systems.

00:24:38.105 --> 00:24:39.902
L want to expand
the holo-projectors

00:24:39.941 --> 00:24:41.568
into all surrounding sections.

00:24:41.609 --> 00:24:44.169
Replicate enough emitters
for the task.

00:24:46.347 --> 00:24:47.939
Yes, sir.

00:25:01.662 --> 00:25:03.653
The holo-emitters
in this corridor are stable.

00:25:03.698 --> 00:25:05.461
Let's start working
on Section 19.

00:25:07.969 --> 00:25:10.802
But first, tell the guard
to escort you to Engineering

00:25:10.838 --> 00:25:13.204
that we need more equipment...

00:25:13.240 --> 00:25:15.834
specifically,
a type-3 isolinear emitter.

00:25:15.876 --> 00:25:17.138
If he gives you any trouble,

00:25:17.178 --> 00:25:20.375
say "l can't complete
the assignment without it."

00:25:22.917 --> 00:25:25.351
We need an isolinear
emitter from Engineering.

00:25:41.569 --> 00:25:43.537
Ensign, how did l get here?

00:25:43.571 --> 00:25:44.663
L transferred you here

00:25:44.705 --> 00:25:46.297
using the new emitters
in this section.

00:25:46.340 --> 00:25:47.466
L assume you've got a plan?

00:25:47.508 --> 00:25:48.475
Half a plan.

00:25:48.509 --> 00:25:49.635
Let's hear it.

00:25:49.677 --> 00:25:51.770
Before we can retake the ship,
we've got to get the crew back.

00:25:51.812 --> 00:25:54.144
And that means disabling
the neural interfaces.

00:25:54.181 --> 00:25:55.648
Easier said than done.

00:25:55.683 --> 00:25:57.514
The great hunters are
everywhere you turn.

00:25:57.551 --> 00:25:58.950
Don't worry.

00:25:58.986 --> 00:26:00.886
L think l've found a way to tap

00:26:00.921 --> 00:26:02.855
into the Sick Bay
diagnostic console.

00:26:02.890 --> 00:26:04.551
The only catch is...

00:26:07.762 --> 00:26:08.786
Stand by with the emitter.

00:26:08.829 --> 00:26:09.818
L'm almost done here.

00:26:14.735 --> 00:26:16.032
The catch, Ensign?

00:26:16.070 --> 00:26:18.061
Somebody's got to be
inside the holodeck

00:26:18.105 --> 00:26:19.936
to engage
the Bridge control relays.

00:26:20.007 --> 00:26:20.939
We're shorthanded.

00:26:21.042 --> 00:26:22.031
L know.

00:26:22.076 --> 00:26:24.806
Well, we've got a Borg
on board, don't we?

00:26:24.845 --> 00:26:26.335
Maybe we can put her
to good use.

00:26:32.119 --> 00:26:34.610
L have been studying
Voyager's database

00:26:34.655 --> 00:26:36.816
looking for our next simulation.

00:26:36.857 --> 00:26:38.757
There are many to choose from.

00:26:38.793 --> 00:26:41.455
These people have
a violent history.

00:26:41.495 --> 00:26:45.056
L believe l've found
a worthy prey:

00:26:45.099 --> 00:26:47.533
The Borg.

00:26:47.568 --> 00:26:49.968
When World War II is over,

00:26:50.037 --> 00:26:51.971
we will recreate
a notorious battle

00:26:52.073 --> 00:26:54.337
known as "Wolf 359."

00:26:54.375 --> 00:26:55.740
L look forward to it.

00:26:55.776 --> 00:26:57.243
L thought you might,

00:26:57.278 --> 00:26:59.212
but if you continue
to disobey me,

00:26:59.246 --> 00:27:01.510
this is one hunt
you will never see.

00:27:01.549 --> 00:27:04.916
You nearly destroyed
two of my favored prey.

00:27:04.952 --> 00:27:06.112
You were careless.

00:27:06.153 --> 00:27:07.780
L've become impatient.

00:27:07.822 --> 00:27:09.722
We penetrated this vessel,

00:27:09.757 --> 00:27:12.191
overcame their defenses

00:27:12.226 --> 00:27:15.923
and in the moment of the kill,
you forced us to stop.

00:27:15.996 --> 00:27:20.660
Now we play
these incessant games.

00:27:20.701 --> 00:27:24.762
It's time we took our trophies
and moved on.

00:27:24.805 --> 00:27:27.239
Your lust for the kill
has blinded you

00:27:27.274 --> 00:27:29.674
like many young hunters.

00:27:29.710 --> 00:27:32.440
If you took the time
to study your prey,

00:27:32.480 --> 00:27:35.313
to understand its behavior,
you might learn something.

00:27:35.349 --> 00:27:37.909
There is nothing to be learned.

00:27:37.952 --> 00:27:39.283
You're wrong.

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:42.221
Each prey exposes us
to another way of life

00:27:42.256 --> 00:27:44.588
and makes us reevaluate
our own.

00:27:44.625 --> 00:27:46.217
Have you considered our future?

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:47.488
What will become of us

00:27:47.528 --> 00:27:50.292
when we have hunted
this territory to exhaustion?

00:27:50.331 --> 00:27:52.856
We will travel
to another part of space,

00:27:52.900 --> 00:27:56.131
search for new prey
as we have always done.

00:27:56.170 --> 00:27:59.662
A way of life that hasn't
changed for a thousand years.

00:27:59.707 --> 00:28:01.265
Why should it?

00:28:01.308 --> 00:28:04.368
Species that don't change...

00:28:04.411 --> 00:28:05.969
die.

00:28:09.183 --> 00:28:11.378
We've lost our way.

00:28:11.418 --> 00:28:15.354
We've allowed our predatory
instincts to dominate us.

00:28:15.389 --> 00:28:17.721
We disperse ourselves
throughout the Quadrant,

00:28:17.758 --> 00:28:20.454
sending ships in all directions.

00:28:20.494 --> 00:28:24.260
We've become
a solitary race, isolated.

00:28:24.298 --> 00:28:27.165
We've spread ourselves
too thin.

00:28:27.201 --> 00:28:29.431
We're no longer a culture.

00:28:29.470 --> 00:28:31.563
We have no identity.

00:28:31.605 --> 00:28:34.267
In another thousand years,

00:28:34.308 --> 00:28:37.141
no one will remember
the name "Hirogen."

00:28:37.178 --> 00:28:40.443
Our people must
come back together,

00:28:40.481 --> 00:28:44.383
combine forces,
rebuild our civilization.

00:28:44.418 --> 00:28:45.817
What of the hunt?

00:28:45.853 --> 00:28:48.219
The hunt will always continue

00:28:48.255 --> 00:28:50.223
but in a new way.

00:28:50.257 --> 00:28:53.886
L intend to transform this ship
into a vast simulation

00:28:53.928 --> 00:28:58.194
populated with a varied
and endless supply of prey.

00:28:58.232 --> 00:29:00.962
In time, this technology
can be duplicated

00:29:01.001 --> 00:29:03.128
for other Hirogen.

00:29:03.170 --> 00:29:07.834
These holodecks will allow us
to hold onto our past

00:29:07.875 --> 00:29:10.070
while we face the future.

00:29:10.110 --> 00:29:13.910
Even if l were persuaded,
others wouldn't be.

00:29:14.014 --> 00:29:15.879
Then you are with me.

00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:21.379
L must continue my research.

00:29:21.422 --> 00:29:23.583
L'll see you tomorrow
on Holodeck 1.

00:29:23.624 --> 00:29:26.218
The Americans are due to invade.

00:29:40.173 --> 00:29:42.141
Remain calm and stay quiet.

00:29:42.175 --> 00:29:43.802
There's a Hirogen
working in the bio-lab.

00:29:43.843 --> 00:29:44.810
He might hear us.

00:29:44.844 --> 00:29:47.039
What's the last
thing you remember?

00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:48.513
An attack.

00:29:48.548 --> 00:29:49.879
The Hirogen vessels...

00:29:49.916 --> 00:29:52.248
they breached our hull
and boarded the ship.

00:29:52.285 --> 00:29:54.913
L was in a phaser fight
on Deck 3.

00:29:54.954 --> 00:29:56.251
L was struck several times.

00:29:56.289 --> 00:29:57.381
That's all l remember.

00:29:57.424 --> 00:29:58.413
Then you have no memory

00:29:58.458 --> 00:29:59.948
of the simulations
in the holodeck?

00:30:00.026 --> 00:30:01.323
None.

00:30:01.361 --> 00:30:02.328
The neural interface

00:30:02.362 --> 00:30:04.091
must be circumventing
your memory centers.

00:30:04.130 --> 00:30:05.222
Neural interface?

00:30:05.265 --> 00:30:06.664
Lt's a subdermal transmitter

00:30:06.699 --> 00:30:08.860
that links your neocortex
to the holodeck.

00:30:08.902 --> 00:30:10.426
In essence,
it makes you believe

00:30:10.470 --> 00:30:12.199
you're a character
within the program.

00:30:12.238 --> 00:30:14.468
Why am l in Sick Bay?

00:30:14.507 --> 00:30:16.771
You were wounded
in the simulation.

00:30:16.810 --> 00:30:21.509
It's my job to patch you
all up and send you back in.

00:30:21.548 --> 00:30:24.381
Half the crew is
under lock and key.

00:30:24.417 --> 00:30:26.977
The rest are fighting for
their lives on the holodeck.

00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:29.079
This has been going
on for 19 days...

00:30:29.122 --> 00:30:32.285
dozens of battle scenarios,
one more brutal than the next.

00:30:32.325 --> 00:30:35.226
You should see what a mess
you were after the Crusades.

00:30:35.261 --> 00:30:37.320
Will l be sent
into another simulation?

00:30:37.363 --> 00:30:40.491
Yes, but this time...
with an advantage.

00:30:43.870 --> 00:30:45.997
L have found a way
to disable the interface

00:30:46.105 --> 00:30:47.766
by remodulating
one of your Borg implants

00:30:47.807 --> 00:30:50.207
to emit a jamming signal.

00:30:50.243 --> 00:30:52.711
Once the Hirogen have brought
you back to the holodeck,

00:30:52.745 --> 00:30:54.770
the jamming signal
will activate within seconds.

00:30:54.814 --> 00:30:56.338
My objective?

00:30:56.382 --> 00:30:58.441
You must find a control panel
inside the holodeck

00:30:58.485 --> 00:31:00.453
and engage
the Bridge access relays.

00:31:00.487 --> 00:31:01.852
That will enable
Ensign Kim and me

00:31:01.888 --> 00:31:04.083
to deactivate
all the neural interfaces.

00:31:04.123 --> 00:31:06.353
After Captain Janeway
and the crew regain awareness,

00:31:06.392 --> 00:31:07.916
you can work with them
to mount a resistance

00:31:07.961 --> 00:31:09.394
against the Hirogen.

00:31:09.429 --> 00:31:11.124
What simulation
will l be entering?

00:31:11.164 --> 00:31:13.962
World War ll...
a 20th century Earth conflict.

00:31:14.033 --> 00:31:15.159
Do you know anything about it?

00:31:15.201 --> 00:31:16.190
Nothing.

00:31:16.236 --> 00:31:17.601
That could be a problem.

00:31:17.637 --> 00:31:20.105
Once the interface is disabled,
you won't remember anything

00:31:20.139 --> 00:31:21.902
about your role
in the simulation.

00:31:21.941 --> 00:31:24.205
Think of it
as a new social setting.

00:31:24.244 --> 00:31:25.973
Do your best to fit in.

00:31:27.313 --> 00:31:28.974
This is the last
neural interface.

00:31:29.048 --> 00:31:31.642
When you've finished with her,
you'll help me replicate more.

00:31:33.386 --> 00:31:35.581
L have to sedate you now.

00:31:49.335 --> 00:31:55.934
That old black magic
has me in its spell

00:31:55.975 --> 00:32:02.744
That old black magic
that you weave so well

00:32:02.782 --> 00:32:09.517
Those icy fingers
up and down my spine

00:32:09.556 --> 00:32:14.289
The same old witchcraft
when your eyes meet...

00:32:22.535 --> 00:32:25.561
l must discontinue
this activity.

00:32:25.605 --> 00:32:27.129
L am not well.

00:32:31.477 --> 00:32:33.308
If the entertainment
is over, l'll be going.

00:32:33.346 --> 00:32:34.404
Stay right there, Commandant.

00:32:34.447 --> 00:32:36.415
L'm sure she's fine.

00:32:36.449 --> 00:32:38.440
Let me talk to her.

00:32:40.753 --> 00:32:42.584
What's wrong?

00:32:42.622 --> 00:32:44.146
L require a glass of water.

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:45.316
Make it a quick one.

00:32:45.358 --> 00:32:47.758
L promised the commandant
you'd be singing till midnight.

00:32:47.794 --> 00:32:50.126
L want to get a lot of
information out of him tonight.

00:32:50.163 --> 00:32:51.187
L am ill.

00:32:51.230 --> 00:32:52.993
Look, l don't care
if you're dying.

00:32:53.099 --> 00:32:54.566
Get back out there.

00:32:54.601 --> 00:32:56.865
L won't.

00:33:02.675 --> 00:33:04.438
Maybe you're right about her.

00:33:04.477 --> 00:33:06.707
The evidence is increasing.

00:33:06.746 --> 00:33:07.838
She was present today

00:33:07.880 --> 00:33:10.314
when our courier was
shot down in the street,

00:33:10.350 --> 00:33:12.477
yet somehow, she was unharmed.

00:33:12.518 --> 00:33:15.487
And now, on the eve
of our liberation,

00:33:15.521 --> 00:33:17.489
she becomes uncooperative.

00:33:17.523 --> 00:33:18.888
Leave this to me.

00:33:31.804 --> 00:33:33.829
Captain...

00:33:33.873 --> 00:33:35.841
At ease.
What's the word?

00:33:35.875 --> 00:33:38.435
There is no word, at least
not from the Resistance

00:33:38.478 --> 00:33:39.945
in Sainte Claire.

00:33:39.979 --> 00:33:42.174
Then we won't get any support
from inside the city.

00:33:42.215 --> 00:33:43.182
You may be underestimating

00:33:43.216 --> 00:33:44.808
the good citizens
of Sainte Claire.

00:33:44.851 --> 00:33:46.546
L spent a summer there
when l was 18.

00:33:46.586 --> 00:33:47.848
Let me guess.

00:33:47.887 --> 00:33:50.515
You ate a few snails,
fell in love with a local girl

00:33:50.556 --> 00:33:52.319
and became an expert
on the city.

00:33:52.358 --> 00:33:55.521
Uh... well...

00:33:55.561 --> 00:33:57.461
Yeah, pretty much like that.

00:33:57.497 --> 00:33:58.725
L see.

00:33:58.765 --> 00:34:01.325
But believe me, Captain,
those people love their town.

00:34:01.367 --> 00:34:02.891
They'll fight for it
and die for it.

00:34:02.935 --> 00:34:04.926
Don't count them out yet.

00:34:05.938 --> 00:34:07.599
All right,

00:34:07.640 --> 00:34:09.904
but l won't count
them in, either.

00:34:09.942 --> 00:34:11.500
We continue as planned...

00:34:11.544 --> 00:34:13.512
an assault from the north
at first light.

00:34:15.782 --> 00:34:19.479
So... who was the mademoiselle?

00:34:22.689 --> 00:34:24.680
Her name was Brigitte.

00:34:24.724 --> 00:34:26.521
Great gams.

00:34:26.559 --> 00:34:27.787
One hell of a temper.

00:34:27.827 --> 00:34:29.351
Sounds like your kind of girl.

00:34:31.097 --> 00:34:36.933
August 29, 1936... 12:17 P.M.

00:34:36.969 --> 00:34:39.529
That's when my train
pulled out of Sainte Claire.

00:34:40.907 --> 00:34:42.465
That's the last time l saw her.

00:34:42.508 --> 00:34:45.671
We wrote to each other
every week for three years.

00:34:45.712 --> 00:34:47.441
Then the war broke out

00:34:47.480 --> 00:34:49.414
and l never heard
from her again.

00:34:49.449 --> 00:34:51.212
Sainte Claire's not a big place.

00:34:51.250 --> 00:34:53.411
She shouldn't be
too hard to find.

00:34:53.453 --> 00:34:54.852
L'm counting on it.

00:34:58.390 --> 00:35:01.291
You'll maintain position here,
20 meters from the front doors.

00:35:01.326 --> 00:35:03.089
Arm yourself
with a submachine gun

00:35:03.128 --> 00:35:04.925
and watch
for any sign of trouble.

00:35:04.963 --> 00:35:05.930
Understood.

00:35:05.964 --> 00:35:07.488
Now, we've observed
a 20-second break

00:35:07.532 --> 00:35:09.432
in the guard rotation
at 4:15 A.M.

00:35:09.468 --> 00:35:10.833
That should give you
and me enough time

00:35:10.869 --> 00:35:11.836
to enter the building

00:35:11.870 --> 00:35:13.394
through the storm window
on the eastern wall.

00:35:13.438 --> 00:35:14.735
When l was there yesterday,

00:35:14.773 --> 00:35:17.037
l saw guards posted
at all three stairways.

00:35:17.075 --> 00:35:18.565
So you'll have to reach
the second floor

00:35:18.610 --> 00:35:19.634
through the elevator shaft.

00:35:19.678 --> 00:35:21.339
The command post is
in the main gallery

00:35:21.380 --> 00:35:22.404
at the end of the hall.

00:35:22.447 --> 00:35:24.347
Once inside,
we plant the charges;

00:35:24.383 --> 00:35:25.577
load the transmitter.

00:35:25.617 --> 00:35:27.050
You'll remain here.

00:35:27.085 --> 00:35:28.552
If something goes wrong
and we're caught,

00:35:28.587 --> 00:35:30.578
destroy all evidence
of the underground...

00:35:30.622 --> 00:35:33.420
our contact lists,
decryption codes... everything.

00:35:33.458 --> 00:35:34.425
Right.

00:35:34.459 --> 00:35:36.051
We leave in one hour.

00:35:47.072 --> 00:35:49.336
This won't make much of a bang.

00:35:49.374 --> 00:35:51.706
You forgot to connect
the detonator.

00:35:51.743 --> 00:35:53.938
L will correct the error.

00:35:53.979 --> 00:35:55.469
It's lucky l found
your little error.

00:35:55.514 --> 00:35:56.981
It might have
undermined our mission.

00:35:57.015 --> 00:35:58.949
Are you having second
thoughts about tonight?

00:35:58.984 --> 00:36:00.144
No.

00:36:00.185 --> 00:36:01.743
Good, because l don't
want any more mistakes.

00:36:01.787 --> 00:36:03.254
There won't be any.

00:36:03.288 --> 00:36:04.778
Let's hope not.

00:36:19.938 --> 00:36:21.565
We've got to stop
meeting like this.

00:36:21.606 --> 00:36:23.597
L managed to grab
a quick scan of Holodeck 1

00:36:23.642 --> 00:36:25.473
and it looks like
Seven of Nine is on the move.

00:36:25.510 --> 00:36:27.068
Are you ready in Sick Bay?

00:36:27.112 --> 00:36:29.706
My Hirogen taskmaster is
working in the bio-lab.

00:36:29.748 --> 00:36:31.079
L'll have access
to the medical console

00:36:31.116 --> 00:36:32.743
for another 20 minutes at least.

00:36:32.784 --> 00:36:34.615
That'll give me enough time
to get to the Bridge and...

00:36:38.957 --> 00:36:40.515
Good afternoon.

00:36:40.559 --> 00:36:42.584
What are you doing in here?

00:36:42.627 --> 00:36:45.118
Trying to get the replicator
system back on line...

00:36:45.163 --> 00:36:47.859
unless you prefer
the emergency rations.

00:36:47.899 --> 00:36:51.096
Personally, l'm getting
tired of synthetic protein.

00:36:51.136 --> 00:36:54.196
You're supposed to be the
finest hunters in the Quadrant.

00:36:54.239 --> 00:36:57.106
Why don't you find us
something a little more tasty?

00:36:57.142 --> 00:36:59.610
Something wrong?

00:36:59.644 --> 00:37:02.909
An unauthorized transmission
was sent from this room.

00:37:03.014 --> 00:37:04.572
What kind of transmission?

00:37:04.616 --> 00:37:06.083
L don't know.

00:37:06.118 --> 00:37:08.018
Maybe you can tell me.

00:37:08.053 --> 00:37:11.079
Well... l was trying
to reroute power

00:37:11.123 --> 00:37:13.284
from the main computer
to the replicators.

00:37:13.325 --> 00:37:15.725
Oh, of course.

00:37:15.761 --> 00:37:19.060
L must have tripped
a communications subroutine.

00:37:19.097 --> 00:37:20.655
Sorry about that.

00:37:20.699 --> 00:37:22.030
Didn't mean to worry you.

00:37:22.067 --> 00:37:23.932
Your people have damaged

00:37:23.969 --> 00:37:25.937
just about every system
on this vessel.

00:37:26.037 --> 00:37:27.026
Accidents are bound to happen.

00:37:27.072 --> 00:37:30.303
Now, if you don't mind,
l'm due on the Bridge.

00:37:30.342 --> 00:37:31.604
Show it to me.

00:37:31.643 --> 00:37:32.610
What?

00:37:32.644 --> 00:37:34.771
L want to see this subroutine.

00:37:34.813 --> 00:37:38.146
Show me what you were doing
when the "accident" occurred.

00:37:38.183 --> 00:37:39.673
Forget it.

00:37:39.718 --> 00:37:41.447
L don't have time.

00:37:44.089 --> 00:37:46.557
Do as l say.

00:37:46.591 --> 00:37:47.785
All right!

00:37:50.996 --> 00:37:52.930
But you'd better
call the Bridge.

00:37:52.964 --> 00:37:56.456
Tell your superior
l'm going to be late...

00:37:56.501 --> 00:37:59.732
that l'm working
under your orders now, not his.

00:37:59.771 --> 00:38:02.001
Go ahead.

00:38:02.040 --> 00:38:03.871
Make the call.

00:38:03.909 --> 00:38:06.207
L don't want to take the blame
for this.

00:38:09.748 --> 00:38:12.046
Report to the Bridge.

00:38:12.083 --> 00:38:14.313
Thanks.

00:39:08.507 --> 00:39:11.237
Set the charges here,
here and there.

00:39:13.545 --> 00:39:14.773
This looks like a message

00:39:14.813 --> 00:39:16.781
from one of their
reconnaissance teams.

00:39:26.358 --> 00:39:30.317
These must be instructions
for troop deployments.

00:39:30.362 --> 00:39:34.162
The Germans must be taking up
new positions outside the city.

00:39:37.068 --> 00:39:38.695
It looks like they're mobilizing

00:39:38.737 --> 00:39:41.365
more troops than our sources
originally expected.

00:40:27.185 --> 00:40:29.710
They're moving armored units
into the valley.

00:40:31.856 --> 00:40:33.983
They must know
the Americans are coming.

00:40:34.092 --> 00:40:35.150
We've got to warn them somehow.

00:40:37.662 --> 00:40:38.651
What are you doing?

00:40:40.865 --> 00:40:43.197
You haven't set the charges.

00:40:43.234 --> 00:40:44.929
What is that?

00:40:44.970 --> 00:40:47.165
L believe it is a transmitter.

00:40:47.205 --> 00:40:49.366
L'm attempting to disable it.

00:40:49.407 --> 00:40:51.398
You're sending a message
to the Nazis.

00:40:51.443 --> 00:40:52.273
No.

00:40:52.310 --> 00:40:53.607
Step away

00:40:53.645 --> 00:40:55.112
or l'll kill you.

00:40:55.146 --> 00:40:56.773
What are you doing?!

00:40:56.815 --> 00:40:58.840
Uh, nothing.
Just running a diagnostic...

00:40:58.883 --> 00:41:00.748
You've accessed
the neural interface controls.

00:41:00.785 --> 00:41:01.911
Stop it immediately.

00:41:01.953 --> 00:41:04.148
L told you... no more mistakes.

00:41:04.189 --> 00:41:06.157
You've just made your last one.

00:41:17.302 --> 00:41:18.929
Seven.

00:41:18.970 --> 00:41:21.336
Captain.

00:41:23.074 --> 00:41:24.200
Listen.

00:41:25.477 --> 00:41:26.501
A targ...

00:41:26.544 --> 00:41:28.341
just beyond that ridge.

00:41:28.380 --> 00:41:29.847
You would hunt down
a simple beast

00:41:29.881 --> 00:41:31.314
even in the midst
of our enemies?

00:41:31.349 --> 00:41:33.510
There is no enemy
as great as hunger!

00:41:36.054 --> 00:41:37.817
Why am l being interrupted?

00:41:37.856 --> 00:41:39.084
The holographic Doctor...

00:41:39.124 --> 00:41:41.183
he's disabled
their Captain's interface.

00:41:41.226 --> 00:41:42.352
How?

00:41:42.394 --> 00:41:44.362
L don't know, but l can't
reestablish the link.

00:41:44.396 --> 00:41:45.693
Send a team to Holodeck 1.

00:41:45.730 --> 00:41:47.322
Remove her from the simulation.

00:42:03.314 --> 00:42:04.804
Hirogen hunters.

00:42:04.849 --> 00:42:07.750
Internal scans show 13 of them
on this holodeck.

00:42:18.529 --> 00:42:20.053
Need a hand, buddy?

00:42:21.399 --> 00:42:23.560
Captain Miller,
Fifth Armored Infantry.

00:42:23.601 --> 00:42:26.069
Welcome to Sainte Claire.

00:42:26.103 --> 00:42:27.593
Get me Artillery Unit
Charlie One.

00:42:27.638 --> 00:42:29.469
Take up positions
along this street

00:42:29.507 --> 00:42:30.974
and start laying down fire.

00:42:35.313 --> 00:42:37.907
The Americans have arrived.

00:42:37.949 --> 00:42:39.940
You circumvented our control!

00:42:39.984 --> 00:42:41.281
How?

00:42:41.319 --> 00:42:43.253
Go to hell!

00:42:43.287 --> 00:42:45.585
Spread out!

00:43:04.475 --> 00:43:05.806
Bobby.

00:43:09.313 --> 00:43:11.645
You owe me a postcard.

00:43:12.783 --> 00:43:14.148
Distance: 800 yards.

00:43:14.185 --> 00:43:16.676
Correct for crosswinds.
Fire at will.

00:43:16.721 --> 00:43:18.120
Take cover, boys!

00:43:18.155 --> 00:43:20.487
Charlie One isn't
known for accuracy!

00:43:20.524 --> 00:43:22.583
L can't access
the ship's systems.

00:43:25.496 --> 00:43:27.191
Didn't you say this
was Nazi headquarters?

00:43:27.231 --> 00:43:28.198
L did.

00:43:28.232 --> 00:43:29.199
Then it would stand to reason

00:43:29.233 --> 00:43:30.291
this building
is being targeted.

00:43:30.334 --> 00:43:31.323
Let's get out of here.

00:43:41.946 --> 00:43:44.414
What happened?

00:43:44.448 --> 00:43:46.973
There was a simulated explosion
in Holodeck 1.

00:43:47.084 --> 00:43:49.314
Somehow it blew out the
holo-grid across three decks.

00:43:49.353 --> 00:43:51.184
Is the program still running?

00:43:51.222 --> 00:43:52.655
Yes.

00:44:12.410 --> 00:44:13.877
What is it?

00:44:13.911 --> 00:44:15.742
Lt looks like a bunker.

00:44:18.249 --> 00:44:19.580
All units, listen up.

00:44:19.617 --> 00:44:20.811
We've just blown the lid

00:44:20.851 --> 00:44:22.944
off of some kind
of secret Nazi compound.

00:44:22.987 --> 00:44:24.614
Converge on my position.

00:44:24.655 --> 00:44:25.952
We're going in.

00:44:28.392 --> 00:44:30.792
The breach opened the simulation
into the surrounding sections.

00:44:30.828 --> 00:44:33.296
L'm picking up holographic
soldiers moving onto Deck 5.

00:44:33.331 --> 00:44:37.324
Shut down the holo-emitters
until we can regain control.

00:44:37.368 --> 00:44:40.394
L can't. The program
controls are off-line.

00:44:41.739 --> 00:44:43.570
You wanted a war?

00:44:43.607 --> 00:44:45.336
Looks like you've got one.

00:44:54.785 --> 00:44:56.650
Take your positions
on the double.

00:44:56.687 --> 00:44:58.018
All right, sir.

00:44:59.423 --> 00:45:01.220
Circle to the left.
